# This file is written automatically by `npx convex dev` — you normally do NOT
# edit it by hand. It is shown here only to document what ends up in
# packages/backend/.env.local. .env.local is gitignored.

# Set by `convex dev`:
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
CONVEX_URL=
CONVEX_SITE_URL=

# No Clerk vars belong in this file. The Convex *deployment* env is a separate
# store, and it is where Clerk's values must go:
#   CLERK_FRONTEND_API_URL        (for convex/auth.config.ts — from
#                                  https://dashboard.clerk.com/apps/setup/convex)
#   CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET  (for convex/http.ts — the webhook's signing secret)
# Set both with `npx convex env set …`; verify with `npx convex env list`.

# Didit identity verification belongs in the same *deployment* env, for the same
# reason: convex/identity.ts and convex/http.ts read process.env on the
# deployment, and `convex dev` does not push this file into it.
#   DIDIT_API_KEY                 (for convex/identity.ts `startSession` — the
#                                  API key from https://business.didit.me)
#   DIDIT_WEBHOOK_SECRET          (for convex/http.ts `/didit-webhook` — the raw
#                                  HMAC-SHA256 secret. Didit does NOT use Svix,
#                                  so this is not a whsec_… Clerk-style secret.)
#   DIDIT_WORKFLOW_ID             (optional — which verification workflow to run)
#   DIDIT_API_URL                 (optional — override the session endpoint;
#                                  defaults to Didit's hosted v2 URL)
# Set them with `npx convex env set …`; verify with `npx convex env list`.
# In the Didit dashboard, point the webhook at
#   https://<your-deployment>.convex.site/didit-webhook

# Outbound email, also on the *deployment* env (convex/email.ts reads
# process.env):
#   RESEND_FROM                   (the verified sending address. Unset ⇒ every
#                                  notice is skipped with a console.error.)
#   RESEND_TEST_MODE              ("false" to actually deliver. ANY other value,
#                                  including unset, keeps test mode ON — so a
#                                  dev deployment cannot mail a real owner, and
#                                  a prod one sends nothing until you set it.)
#   APP_URL                       (where apps/web is, e.g. http://localhost:3001
#                                  in dev. Emails append a link built from it;
#                                  unset ⇒ link-free emails, which still read
#                                  correctly. NOT CONVEX_SITE_URL — that is this
#                                  deployment's own origin, and using it would
#                                  mail people a link to the backend.)
#   CONSOLE_URL                   (where apps/admin is. Only a staff invitation
#                                  links there; unset ⇒ the invitation is still
#                                  created and the console says the link was
#                                  not sent. A separate origin from APP_URL, so
#                                  it cannot be a path under it.)
# Set them with `npx convex env set …`; verify with `npx convex env list`.
# Both URLs can also be set from the console's Integrations screen, which wins
# over these — see `model/settings.ts`.

# Escrowed heir release, on the *deployment* env (convex/escrow.ts,
# release.ts). See AGENTS.md "Escrowed release".
#   ESCROW_BACKEND                ("dev" or "gcp". Unset ⇒ "dev".)
#   ESCROW_KEY_ID                 (the key bundles must be locked with: "dev-1"
#                                  in dev, the Cloud KMS key version's resource
#                                  name in prod. Must match apps/mobile/lib/escrow-key.ts.)
#   ESCROW_DEV_PRIVATE_KEY        (dev only — the PKCS#8 DER private key as ONE
#                                  base64 line. A multi-line PEM keeps only its
#                                  first line through `npx convex env set` on
#                                  Windows.)
#   WASSIYA_ENV                   ("production" on prod — refuses the dev key
#                                  and the seed fast-forward helpers.)
#   GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT           (prod — the service-account JSON key as ONE
#                                  base64 line; roles/cloudkms.cryptoKeyDecrypter
#                                  on the escrow key only.)
#   IDENTITY_HASH_SECRET          (≥ 32 chars — the HMAC key ID numbers are
#                                  hashed under. Changing it breaks every match.)
#
# Heir outreach (convex/outreach.ts). Unset ⇒ staff send links by hand.
#   OUTREACH_PROVIDER             ("twilio" to send SMS)
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN
#   TWILIO_FROM                   (a sender number, or a Messaging Service "MG…")
